    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0381" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.54262/308: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-09T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1922—11
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>92. Department’s 61 May 6, 3 p.m. I handed to Von Haniel<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d221-f1"/> yesterday a note dated May 8th containing the text of the
                    Department’s notification.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Houghton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d221-f1" n="10" xml:id="d221-f1-content">
                <p>German Secretary of State in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
